### Stage 1 Gate (verified 2026-08-23)
- [x] Finish every phase and required verification in the current stage before
  beginning implementation in the next stage.
- [x] Within each stage, stabilize migrations/models, repository/service policy,
  handlers/protocols, and adversarial tests before adding user or operator UI.
- [x] Build UI only from shared Skaia primitives and complete loading, empty,
  denied, stale, error, success, responsive, keyboard, and screen-reader states.
- [x] Keep provider-specific language and behavior inside optional adapters;
  core routes, entities, permissions, feature flags, and UI labels stay generic
  and tenant-configurable.
- [x] After every stage, update affected specs and this tip with verification,
  newly discovered dependencies, and the next unblocked stage.

Reset and re-verify these gates for each subsequent stage before advancing.

### Stage 2 Gate (verified 2026-08-23)
- [x] Completed backend health/status/incident authority before operator/public UI.
- [x] Kept public disclosure generic and operator telemetry policy-protected.
- [x] Passed backup integrity, isolated restore/readiness, release, bounded HTTP,
  WebSocket reconnect, backend race, frontend state/accessibility, and spec gates.
- [x] Recorded the legacy superuser application-login deployment dependency in
  the existing soft-delete rollout handoff; it is not hidden by readiness.

### Next Steps
- [x] 2026-08-23: Completed `db_transactions_concurrency` with checkout/provider
  idempotency, transition guards, durable fulfilment leases and recovery,
  atomic payouts, and PostgreSQL/race-backed concurrency verification.
- [x] 2026-08-23: Completed `production_readiness_and_service_status` with
